@* The public front page: what this is, who it's for, and how to get in. No made-up testimonials. *@
<div class="landing">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-text">
            <p class="eyebrow">@AppOptions.AppName</p>
            <h1 id="hero-title">Every family has stories worth keeping.</h1>
            <p class="hero-lead">Each week, the people you love get one gentle question about their life. They answer by typing, by talking, or with a photo, and the family ends up with a library of their stories, a family tree, and a real printed book.</p>
            <div class="button-row">
                <a class="button button-primary button-large" href="/account/login">Sign in</a>
                <a class="button button-secondary" href="#how-it-works">See how it works</a>
            </div>
            <p class="muted">Invited by a family member? Tap the button in their email. There's no password to remember.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-card" aria-hidden="true">
            <p class="mock-eyebrow">This week's question</p>
            <p class="mock-question">What games did you play, and who were your childhood friends?</p>
            <div class="mock-lines"><span></span><span></span><span class="short"></span></div>
            <div class="mock-buttons"><span class="mock-record">Record my voice</span><span class="mock-photo">Add photos</span></div>
            <p class="mock-saved">Saved ✓ 2:41 PM</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="how-it-works" class="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
        <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
        <ol class="steps-grid">
            <li>
                <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
                <h3>One question a week</h3>
                <p>52 warm, thoughtful questions, from "Where were you born?" to "What do you want your great-grandchildren to know?" Each arrives by email with one big button. No apps to install.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
                <h3>Answer your way</h3>
                <p>Type it, say it out loud, or add old photos and letters. Grandchildren can sit beside Grandma and write it down for her. Everything saves itself as you go.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
                <h3>Keep it forever</h3>
                <p>The stories become a family library to browse, a website that works from a USB stick, and a book ready for Lulu or Amazon to print.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
        <h2 id="features-title">Made for the whole family</h2>
        <ul class="feature-grid">
            <li><h3>Made for grandparents</h3><p>Big, clear text you can make bigger. Large buttons with words on them. One question per screen. Signing in is a tap on an email link, or a QR code on a printed card.</p></li>
            <li><h3>Their voice, saved</h3><p>One tap records their voice. Decades from now, the family can still hear Grandpa laugh as he tells the story about the county fair.</p></li>
            <li><h3>Photos and the family tree</h3><p>Add photos straight from an iPhone, say who's in them, and see every story connected to the people in a simple family tree. GEDCOM import and export included.</p></li>
            <li><h3>Private by design</h3><p>It runs on your own server, not someone else's cloud. Every storyteller chooses who can read each story: everyone, a few people, or only themselves.</p></li>
            <li><h3>A real book</h3><p>Print-ready interior and cover PDFs with page numbers, a table of contents, photos, the family tree, and QR codes that play the recordings.</p></li>
            <li><h3>Safe for decades</h3><p>Encrypted backups every night, checked every week, with a complete archive in open formats so the stories outlive any app.</p></li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="roles" aria-labelledby="roles-title">
        <h2 id="roles-title">Who does what</h2>
        <div class="roles-grid">
            <div><h3>Storytellers</h3><p>Grandparents, parents, great-aunts. They answer the questions, at their own pace.</p></div>
            <div><h3>Family</h3><p>Children, grandchildren and cousins read the stories, leave a ♥ or a note, and ask follow-up questions.</p></div>
            <div><h3>A family admin</h3><p>One helpful person sets it up, invites everyone, and is the "Need help?" phone number on every page.</p></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
        <h2 id="closing-title">The best time to ask is now.</h2>
        <p>Ask your family admin for an invitation, or sign in if you already have one.</p>
        <a class="button button-primary button-large" href="/account/login">Sign in</a>
    </section>
</div>
